    "trigger_card_number": 832,
    "title": "LECCIÓN 67: LAS SEÑALES DEL TEXTO",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "La escritura formal avisa al lector de",
          "adónde va. Estas son las señales.",
          "",
          "Añadir: moreover, furthermore,",
          "in addition.",
          "Contrastar: however, nevertheless,",
          "whereas, conversely.",
          "Concluir: hence, therefore, thus,",
          "consequently."
        ]
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Para enmarcar un tema:",
          "in terms of = en cuanto a.",
          "with regard to / as regards = respecto a.",
          "from a ... perspective = desde un punto",
          "de vista.",
          "",
          "\"From a broader perspective, the",
          "decision was not merely rash; it was",
          "inevitable.\"",
          "",
          "Resultado con propósito: thereby + -ing.",
          "\"cutting costs, thereby saving the site\"",
          "",
          "whereas une dos cláusulas en UNA frase;",
          "however une dos frases.",
          "",
          "El español encadena con conectores muy",
          "parecidos; el inglés exige la coma tras ellos."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "068",
    "trigger_word": "classroom",
    "trigger_card_number": 901,
    "title": "LECCIÓN 68: SO DO I",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Al inglés no le gusta repetirse. Deja",
          "fuera la segunda mitad, o mete una",
          "palabra corta en su lugar.",
          "",
          "Coincidir: so + auxiliar + sujeto.",
          "\"I liked it.\" \"So did I.\"",
          "Coincidir en negativo:",
          "\"I don't smoke.\" \"Neither do I.\"",
          "",
          "Fíjate en la inversión tras so y",
          "neither."
        ]
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "one / ones sustituye a un sustantivo",
          "contable:",
          "\"Our classroom has no windows, and",
          "neither does the one next door.\"",
          "",
          "do so / do it sustituye a todo un",
          "sintagma verbal:",
          "\"She asked him to wait, and he did so.\"",
          "",
          "Y a veces se omite todo:",
          "\"Coming?\" \"If not, tell me.\" \"Why?\"",
          "",
          "Omite solo lo que el otro pueda",
          "reponer. En la duda, dilo.",
          "",
          "El español calla el sujeto sin más; el",
          "inglés necesita que el auxiliar se",
          "quede como suplente."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
